6. Admissibility Algebra

Definition 6 (Provenance structure). A provenance structure is a quadruple (D, \preceq, \alpha, \tau) where D is a finite set of documents, \preceq \;\subseteq D \times D is a relation with x \preceq y read "x cites or derives from y," \alpha: D \to 2^{F} assigns to each document the set of facts it asserts, and \tau: D \to \{A, B\} is the source-quality grade with A denoting primary and B secondary. A document x is primary iff \tau(x) = A.

Definition 7 (Derivation and tier-T closure). For S \subseteq D, a fact f \in F is derivable at tier T from S if there exists a finite rooted tree with root labelled f, leaves in S, internal nodes labelled by documents in D, each edge oriented along \preceq, and every internal node y satisfying \tau(y) \ge T in the order A > B. The tier-T closure of S is

\operatorname{Cl}_T(S) = \{ f \in F : f \text{ is derivable at tier } T \text{ from } S \}.

The tier-T admissible document set is

\mathcal{A}_T(S) = \{ x \in D : \alpha(x) \subseteq \operatorname{Cl}_T(S) \}.

The tier convention is part of Definition 7, not a post hoc addition: the grade of every internal document, including those that have themselves been admitted, is constrained by T, so a derivation via an admitted document does not escape the tier restriction.

Theorem 5 (Closure operator). For each T \in \{A, B\}, the map S \mapsto \mathcal{A}_T(S) is a closure operator on the lattice (2^{D}, \subseteq): it is extensive, monotone, and idempotent.

Proof. Extensive: each x \in S is derivable from itself at depth zero with an empty set of internal documents, so the tier constraint is vacuously satisfied and x \in \mathcal{A}_T(S). Monotone: if S \subseteq S', any derivation tree from S is a derivation tree from S' with the same internal documents and the same tier restriction, so \operatorname{Cl}_T(S) \subseteq \operatorname{Cl}_T(S') and hence \mathcal{A}_T(S) \subseteq \mathcal{A}_T(S'). Idempotent: suppose x \in \mathcal{A}_T(\mathcal{A}_T(S)). Then \alpha(x) is derivable at tier T from \mathcal{A}_T(S), so there is a tree with internal nodes of grade at least T and leaves in \mathcal{A}_T(S). Each leaf y \in \mathcal{A}_T(S) satisfies \alpha(y) \subseteq \operatorname{Cl}_T(S), so there is a tree with internal nodes of grade at least T and leaves in S. Substituting each leaf's tree into the tree for \alpha(x) yields a tree for \alpha(x) with all internal nodes of grade at least T and leaves in S. The tier constraint is preserved because both composing trees respect it, and no internal node is downgraded by substitution. Hence \alpha(x) \subseteq \operatorname{Cl}_T(S) and x \in \mathcal{A}_T(S). \square

The convention that the tier restriction applies to internal nodes as well as to the root is what makes idempotence hold without an auxiliary source-quality argument.

Corollary 4 (Audit monotonicity). The audit quantities

N_{\text{adm}}(S) = |\mathcal{A}^{\text{strict}}(S)|, \qquad
N_{\text{labs}}(S) = \big|\{ d(i) : i \in \mathcal{A}^{\text{strict}}(S) \}\big|, \qquad
p_{\text{indep}}(S) = \frac{|\{ i \in \mathcal{A}^{\text{strict}}(S) : \tau(\text{docs}_i) = A \}|}{N_{\text{adm}}(S)}

satisfy N_{\text{adm}}(S) \le N_{\text{adm}}(S') and N_{\text{labs}}(S) \le N_{\text{labs}}(S') whenever S \subseteq S'. The threshold event \{N_{\text{adm}} \ge N_{\text{adm}}^*,\ N_{\text{labs}} \ge N_{\text{labs}}^*,\ p_{\text{indep}} \ge p_{\text{indep}}^*\} is therefore monotone in the record: adding documents cannot convert a pass into a fail.

Proof. Immediate from monotonicity of \mathcal{A}_T and the fact that cardinality and developer-projection are monotone under inclusion. The last clause follows because the conjunction of lower bounds is preserved under non-decreasing arguments. \square

Corollary 5 (Pilot insufficiency). Let S_{\text{pilot}} be the document set for a pilot of n_{\text{pilot}} releases. Then N_{\text{adm}}(S_{\text{pilot}}) \le n_{\text{pilot}}. If n_{\text{pilot}} < N_{\text{adm}}^*, the pilot cannot certify the threshold N_{\text{adm}} \ge N_{\text{adm}}^* for any outcome.

Proof. Each admitted release requires at least one document asserting its deployment date, so |\mathcal{A}^{\text{strict}}(S_{\text{pilot}})| \le n_{\text{pilot}}. \square

Definition 8 (Freeze operator). Let \Theta = (N_{\text{adm}}^*, N_{\text{labs}}^*, p_{\text{indep}}^*, g_0, \bar{g}, \Lambda, B, \alpha). A freeze at time t_f replaces \Theta by \Theta_{t_f} and prohibits any subsequent map \Theta_{t_f} \mapsto \Theta_{t} for t > t_f that depends on the observed Z.

