10. Algorithms

The following procedures are stated formally, with correctness and complexity statements. They are mathematical specifications, not implementations; no code is executed and no data are processed.

Algorithm 1 (Provenance closure).
Input: (D, \preceq, \alpha, \tau), seed set S \subseteq D, tier T.
Output: \mathcal{A}_T(S).
Procedure: (1) Initialise a queue with S and an accumulated fact set F_{\text{acc}} with \bigcup_{x \in S} \alpha(x). (2) While the queue is non-empty, pop y, and for each x with x \preceq y and \tau(x) \ge T, add \alpha(x) to F_{\text{acc}} and enqueue x. (3) Return \{x \in D : \alpha(x) \subseteq F_{\text{acc}}\}.
Correctness: by construction F_{\text{acc}} = \operatorname{Cl}_T(S), so the returned set equals \mathcal{A}_T(S) by Definition 7. Complexity: O(|D| + |{\preceq}|) time, O(|D| + |F|) space.

Algorithm 2 (Sharp bounds and breakdown).
Input: counts (n_{g}, n_{g, Z=1})_{g \in \{L, H\}}, bound \Lambda.
Output: \Pi_L(\Lambda), \Pi_H(\Lambda), \Delta interval, \Lambda^{*}.
Procedure: compute p_g = n_{g,Z=1}/n_g; set \Pi_g by Theorem 4, handling the zero-cell case; set the \Delta interval by Corollary 3; compute \Lambda^{*} by Proposition 2 (or by solving \underline{\Delta}(\Lambda) = 0 and \overline{\Delta}(\Lambda) = 0 and taking the smaller feasible root, with \Lambda^{*} = \infty if no root exists).
Correctness: Theorems 4, Corollary 3, Proposition 2. Complexity: O(1) arithmetic operations.

Algorithm 3 (Joint-law sharp bound).
Input: observed marginals p_L, p_H, assumed joint feasibility constraints, bound \Lambda.
Output: sharp \Delta interval under the assumed joint.
Procedure: solve the linear programme of Proposition 1 by enumerating vertices of the polytope; the objective is linear in the four-way table, so the extrema are at vertices.
Correctness: Proposition 1. Complexity: polynomial in the number of table cells, which is constant (sixteen cells), hence O(1) in the sample size.

Algorithm 4 (Stratified studentised permutation with orbit check and CI inversion).
Input: strata data (Z_k, W_k)_{k=1}^{K}, replicates B, level \alpha, grid \mathcal{G}_{\Delta}.
Output: feasibility flag, p_{\text{perm}}, and a confidence set.
Procedure: (0) compute |\Omega(W)| = \prod_k \binom{n_k}{n_{1k}}; if |\Omega(W)| < 1/\alpha, return randomization test infeasible at level \alpha and skip steps (1)–(4). (1) compute T(W, Z); (2) for b = 1, \ldots, B, draw W^{(b)} uniformly from \Omega(W), compute T(W^{(b)}, Z); (3) set p_{\text{perm}} = B^{-1}\sum_b \mathbf{1}\{|T^{(b)}| \ge |T|\}; (4) for each \delta \in \mathcal{G}_{\Delta}, compute T_\delta centred at \delta and the permutation quantile q_{1-\alpha}^{\text{perm}}(\delta), retain \delta if |T_\delta| \le q_{1-\alpha}^{\text{perm}}(\delta).
Correctness: Theorem 6 (exactness and orbit feasibility); the inversion gives a set whose coverage follows from the duality between tests and confidence sets under the sharp null. Complexity: O(Bn) per grid point, O(Bn|\mathcal{G}_{\Delta}|) total, plus O(K) for the orbit check.

Algorithm 5 (Audit decision).
Input: frozen document set S, frozen parameters \Theta_{t_f}.
Output: a pass/fail decision and a disclosure-gap report.
Procedure: compute N_{\text{adm}}, N_{\text{labs}}, p_{\text{indep}} by Algorithm 1 and count; compare to thresholds; if fail, compute the missing-field histogram, the proportion of releases lacking an admitted start–deployment pair, the orbit size and its feasibility, and the list of specific regime changes that would close the gap.
Correctness: the decision is a deterministic function of (S, \Theta_{t_f}) by definition. Complexity: O(|D| + |{\preceq}|).

Algorithm 6 (MDE precomputation).
Input: target n, level \alpha, power 1-\beta, approximation flag.
Output: \rho_{\min}(n), either Fisher or exact.
Procedure: if Fisher, evaluate Theorem 7; if exact, compute \pi_n(\rho, \alpha) from the hypergeometric distribution of permutation ranks and invert by binary search.
Correctness: Theorem 7 for Fisher; Remark 4 for exact. Complexity: O(1) for Fisher, O(n \log(n)) for exact.

Algorithm 7 (Rival-set sensitivity).
Input: record S, frozen rival sets \{\mathcal{R}_i^{\text{frozen}}\}, window h.
Output: \Theta^{\text{frozen}}(\Lambda), \Theta^{\text{dyn}}(\Lambda; h), fragility index \Phi(h).
Procedure: compute G_i^{\text{frozen}} and G_i^{\text{dyn}}(h); run Algorithm 2 under each; compute \Phi(h) by Definition 5.
Correctness: Definitions 4–5. Complexity: O(|\mathcal{R}|^2) for the pairwise comparisons.

