Appendix A. Notation and Conventions

A.1 Sets and indices. $\mathcal{R}$ finite set of releases; $\mathcal{D}$ finite set of developers; $d(i)\in\mathcal{D}$ developer of $i$. $\mathcal{A}\subseteq\mathcal{R}$ releases with admitted deployment date $t_i^B$; $\mathcal{A}^S\subseteq\mathcal{A}$ releases with admitted start date $s_i$. $\mathcal{R}_i\subseteq\mathcal{R}\setminus\{i\}$ frozen rival set at freeze date $t_f$. $\mathcal{R}_i^{\mathrm{dyn}}(h)=\{j\neq i:|t_j-t_i|\le h\}$ dynamic rival set for sensitivity analysis (Definition 4). $\mathcal{G}_L,\mathcal{G}_H$ low- and high-pressure groups defined by frozen threshold $g_0$ on $G_i$; $L,H$ are abbreviations.

A.2 Latent and observed variables. $s_i\in\mathbb{R}_+$ evaluation start; $c_i\in(0,\infty]$ absolute completion time; $\tau_i=c_i-s_i\in(0,\infty]$ evaluation duration, $\infty$ permitted; $t_i^B\in\mathbb{R}_+$ broad deployment. $Y_i=\mathbf{1}\{\tau_i<t_i^B-s_i\}$ completion before deployment; $M_i\in\{0,1\}$ disclosure indicator; $Z_i=M_iY_i$ observed outcome. The record reveals $Z_i$, never $(M_i,Y_i)$ separately. $u_i$ capacity type, $\iota_i$ independence regime, $a_i$ access level, all latent. $\mathrm{docs}_i\subseteq D$ provenance-annotated document set. The exposure is $G_i=s_i-\max\{t_j:j\in\mathcal{R}_i,\ t_j\le s_i\}$ when the defining set is non-empty, and $G_i=\bar{g}$ otherwise, with $\bar{g}\in\Theta_{t_f}$ a frozen parameter. Every $G$-theorem is conditioned on $i\in\mathcal{A}^S$.

A.3 Parameters. $\Lambda\in[0,\infty]$ bounds the undisclosed odds $\lambda_g=P(M=0,Y=1\mid\mathcal{G}_g)/P(M=1,Y=1\mid\mathcal{G}_g)$ (Assumption A5). $\Lambda^*$ is the breakdown bound (Definition 3). $p_g=P(Z=1\mid\mathcal{G}_g)$ observed; $\pi_g=P(Y=1\mid\mathcal{G}_g)$ latent; $\Delta=\pi_L-\pi_H$. $\Theta=(N_{\mathrm{adm}}^*,N_{\mathrm{labs}}^*,p_{\mathrm{indep}}^*,g_0,\bar{g},\Lambda,B,\alpha)$ is frozen after instrument calibration (A7); $\Theta_{t_f}$ is its frozen value at $t_f$. $\Phi(h)$ is the fragility index (Definition 5).

A.4 Tier and provenance. Documents $x\in D$ carry grade $\tau(x)\in\{A,B\}$ with $A>B$. A derivation tree for fact $f$ is a finite rooted tree with root $f$, leaves in seed $S$, internal nodes $y\in D$ satisfying $\tau(y)\ge T$, and edges oriented along $\preceq$. The tier-$T$ closure is $\mathrm{Cl}_T(S)=\{f:f\text{ derivable at tier }T\text{ from }S\}$; the tier-$T$ admissible set is $\mathcal{A}_T(S)=\{x:\alpha(x)\subseteq\mathrm{Cl}_T(S)\}$. The tier convention constrains every internal node, including already-admitted documents, which is what makes idempotence hold without an auxiliary source-quality argument.

