Appendix D. Proofs for Section 6

D.1 Theorem 5 (Closure operator)

For each $T\in\{A,B\}$, the map $S\mapsto\mathcal{A}_T(S)$ is extensive, monotone, and idempotent on $(2^D,\subseteq)$.

Proof. Extensive: every $x\in S$ derives each $f\in\alpha(x)$ from leaf $x$ with an empty internal set, so the tier constraint is vacuous and $x\in\mathcal{A}_T(S)$. Monotone: a derivation tree from $S$ is a derivation tree from any $S'\supseteq S$ with the same internal documents, so $\mathrm{Cl}_T(S)\subseteq\mathrm{Cl}_T(S')$ and hence $\mathcal{A}_T(S)\subseteq\mathcal{A}_T(S')$. Idempotent: let $x\in\mathcal{A}_T(\mathcal{A}_T(S))$. For each $f\in\alpha(x)$ there is a tree $\mathcal{T}_f$ with leaves in $\mathcal{A}_T(S)$ and internal nodes of grade at least $T$. Each leaf $y\in\mathcal{A}_T(S)$ has $\alpha(y)\subseteq\mathrm{Cl}_T(S)$ via a tree $\mathcal{U}_{y,g}$ whose internal nodes also have grade at least $T$. Substituting $\mathcal{U}_{y,g}$ for each leaf $y$ in $\mathcal{T}_f$ yields a tree with leaves in $S$ whose internal nodes are internal nodes of the original trees; no internal node is downgraded, so the tier constraint is preserved. Hence $f\in\mathrm{Cl}_T(S)$ and $x\in\mathcal{A}_T(S)$. $\square$

D.2 Corollary 4 (Audit monotonicity)

If $S\subseteq S'$, then $N_{\mathrm{adm}}(S)\le N_{\mathrm{adm}}(S')$ and $N_{\mathrm{labs}}(S)\le N_{\mathrm{labs}}(S')$, and the threshold event $\{N_{\mathrm{adm}}\ge N_{\mathrm{adm}}^*,\ N_{\mathrm{labs}}\ge N_{\mathrm{labs}}^*,\ p_{\mathrm{indep}}\ge p_{\mathrm{indep}}^*\}$ is monotone in the record: adding documents cannot convert a pass into a fail.

Proof. Immediate from monotonicity of $\mathcal{A}_T$, the monotonicity of cardinality and developer-projection under inclusion, and the preservation of conjunctions of lower bounds under non-decreasing arguments. $\square$

D.3 Corollary 5 (Pilot insufficiency)

For a pilot of $n_{\mathrm{pilot}}$ releases, $N_{\mathrm{adm}}(S_{\mathrm{pilot}})\le n_{\mathrm{pilot}}$. If $n_{\mathrm{pilot}}<N_{\mathrm{adm}}^*$, the pilot cannot certify the threshold for any outcome.

Proof. Each admitted release requires at least one document asserting its deployment date, so $|\mathcal{A}^{\mathrm{strict}}(S_{\mathrm{pilot}})|\le n_{\mathrm{pilot}}$. $\square$

